# EXPRESS-013 manual requests. Send them from top to bottom.
# 1. Start the server: npm run dev:express:13  (starts with notes n1 … n4)
# 2. Click "Send Request" above a request (VS Code extension "REST Client").
# Saving task13.ts restarts the server and brings the notes back.

@host = http://localhost:3000

### Bob edits Alice's private note, he can't see it (expect 404)
PATCH {{host}}/notes/n1
Authorization: Bearer token-bob
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hacked" }

### Bob edits Alice's team note, he can see it but it is not his (expect 403)
PATCH {{host}}/notes/n2
Authorization: Bearer token-bob
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hacked" }

### Invalid title from the owner (expect 400)
PATCH {{host}}/notes/n2
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### Owner changes visibility, ownerId is ignored (expect 200, ownerId still "u-alice")
PATCH {{host}}/notes/n1
Authorization: Bearer token-alice
Content-Type: application/json

{ "visibility": "team", "ownerId": "u-bob" }

### Admin edits Bob's private note (expect 200)
PATCH {{host}}/notes/n3
Authorization: Bearer token-root
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Edited by admin" }

### Bob deletes Alice's team note (expect 403)
DELETE {{host}}/notes/n2
Authorization: Bearer token-bob

### Owner deletes own note (expect 204)
DELETE {{host}}/notes/n4
Authorization: Bearer token-bob

### Deleted note is gone (expect 404)
DELETE {{host}}/notes/n4
Authorization: Bearer token-bob
